WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:15.581
"Happy needs to go for a walk," says Mother.

2
00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:18.626
"Take him for a walk around the neighborhood.

3
00:00:18.627 --> 00:00:21.506
Here's a basket and a shopping list.

4
00:00:21.507 --> 00:00:25.407
Please get everything on the list for dinner."

5
00:00:25.408 --> 00:00:29.533
So now, Happy and I are walking down the street.

6
00:00:29.534 --> 00:00:31.943
Happy is wagging his tail.

7
00:00:31.944 --> 00:00:35.423
He loves going for a walk around the neighborhood.

8
00:00:35.424 --> 00:00:37.885
All the store owners know us.

9
00:00:37.886 --> 00:00:43.985
And Happy loves all the strange and wonderful smells.

10
00:00:43.986 --> 00:00:46.779
First, I go into the bakery.

11
00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:52.818
Mrs. Thompson always gives me a cookie with lots of chocolate chips.

12
00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:55.316
I buy some garlic bread.

13
00:00:55.317 --> 00:01:00.507
"Bye, Mrs. Thompson. Thank you!" I say.

14
00:01:00.508 --> 00:01:03.614
There's Mr. James, the butcher.

15
00:01:03.615 --> 00:01:06.700
He's always singing Italian songs.

16
00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:08.880
He wears a white apron.

17
00:01:08.881 --> 00:01:14.761
He sells all kinds of meat: pork, beef, and chicken.

18
00:01:14.762 --> 00:01:17.290
He throws Happy a bone.

19
00:01:17.291 --> 00:01:20.428
Happy loves the butcher shop!

20
00:01:20.429 --> 00:01:24.785
My favorite store is Purdy's Chocolate House.

21
00:01:24.786 --> 00:01:28.127
The girl who works there goes to my school.

22
00:01:28.128 --> 00:01:30.551
She is in grade seven.

23
00:01:30.552 --> 00:01:33.544
Her mom makes the best fudge.

24
00:01:33.545 --> 00:01:39.769
Sometimes she lets me lick the spoon.

25
00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:43.296
We have two more things to get for Mommy:

26
00:01:43.297 --> 00:01:45.847
fish and cucumbers.

27
00:01:45.848 --> 00:01:49.984
Happy and I go to the fish market down by the river.

28
00:01:49.985 --> 00:01:54.135
The men at the fish market call out to the customers,

29
00:01:54.136 --> 00:01:56.964
"Salmon! Two big ones!"

30
00:01:56.965 --> 00:02:02.445
"Hi, Jimmy, how's Happy?" the man asks.

31
00:02:02.446 --> 00:02:07.071
At the vegetable market, the cucumbers are in a basket.

32
00:02:07.072 --> 00:02:11.638
Mrs. Sanderson wipes off two cucumbers with a towel.

33
00:02:11.639 --> 00:02:14.947
Then she puts them in a brown paper bag.

34
00:02:14.948 --> 00:02:17.478
She also gives me an orange.

35
00:02:17.479 --> 00:02:22.074
"Here you go, Jimmy!" she says.

36
00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:27.166
When we get home, Mommy is very pleased with our shopping.

37
00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:31.734
"Did the people in our neighborhood help you?" she asks.

38
00:02:31.735 --> 00:02:34.777
"Yes, they did," I say.

39
00:02:34.778 --> 00:02:37.613
"I got a cookie and an orange.

40
00:02:37.614 --> 00:02:40.746
And Happy got a bone!"
